  "raw": {
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34676": {
      "title": "Clinical Research-Focus Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Clinical Research-Focus Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Clinical Research-Focus Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The expected start date is summer 2027 (preference for August). Applications will be reviewed beginning December 1, 2026, but will be reviewed until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Details Title Clinical Research-Focus Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow Specific Title Postdoctoral Fellow in Psychiatry Appointment Type Postdoctoral Fellow Department IUSM - Psychiatry Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary Clinical Research-Focus Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow Teen POWER – Indiana University School of Medicine The Teen Program Of Weight and Eating Research (Teen POWER ) at the Indiana University School of Medicine is seeking qualified candidates for one to two clinical-research-focused Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow position. Patient-oriented treatment research funded by NIH as well as pilot studies will provide advanced clinical-research opportunities for individuals interested in academic careers working with eating/weight disorders or adolescent behavioral health. This full-time position is 100% research effort (and therefore eligible for NIH loan repayment programs), but day-to-day activities will involve approximately 40% research activities and 60% clinical activities (therapy/assessment) delivered in the context of clinical trials. Clinical activities (60%) will involve serving as a research clinician performing assessments and providing evidence-based treatment on an NIH -funded randomized controlled trial treating adolescents with binge eating, as well as pilot studies. The postdoc will receive intensive training and ongoing supervision in the administration of diagnostic and semi-structured interviews (e.g., Eating Disorder Examination). as well as the delivery of evidence-based treatments (i.e., CBT - LOC , IHBLT ) for eating/weight disorders. Additional pilot studies are planned and will involve similar activities. Research activities (40%) will involve data analysis, preparing data reports for grant progress reports and new grant applications, and submitting research papers for publication and presentation at conferences. Data from numerous completed treatment and longitudinal studies on eating/weight disorders will also be available for research projects and publications. The postdoc will also supervise/mentor research staff (e.g., postbac and graduate student research assistants) in data management activities. Candidates must have a doctoral degree in psychology, a completed APA -accredited internship, and experience working with eating/weight disorders and adolescents/families. Experience in data management systems (e.g., REDCap, Qualtrics) and strong statistical skills and experiences, and excellent writing skills (including publications in peer-reviewed journals) are required. This position is tailor-made for loan repayment program applications. It is ideal for individuals pursuing academic clinical-research careers, with a focus on research (e.g., tenure-track faculty) or clinical track (e.g., staff psychologist or clinical service director). The position offers intensive mentored opportunities for publishing and grant-writing. Working at Teen POWER Teen POWER is a new research clinic in the Department of Psychiatry. Our program received funding from the NIH to conduct treatment studies for adolescents with eating/weight concerns, building upon a six-year track record conducting similar behavioral clinical trials. Teen POWER is best suited for individuals who are curious and patient-centered. Teen POWER offers an ideal research environment to engage with colleagues about clinical observations, data results, and their significance. Beyond having a strong work ethic and being detail-oriented, Teen POWER prioritizes highly collaborative and collegial relationships with peers and faculty, who make it a point to be highly responsive and accessible. The Department of Psychiatry has a broad research, clinical, and teaching mission and maintains a clinical psychology internship, a psychiatry residency program, and fellowships in addition to training rotations for medical and graduate students. Indiana University School of Medicine is the largest medical school in the United States, with a large academic health center in downtown Indianapolis, the 17th largest city in the United States. In addition to having active sports, cultural, arts, and educational events and programs, Indianapolis is located centrally near several other major cities including Chicago, Louisville, Cincinnati, and Columbus. IU School of Medicine is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. IU School of Medicine is closely aligned with our health system partner, IU Health, which has twice earned a place on the US News and World Report Honor Roll. The shared vision of both institutions is to lead the transformation of healthcare through quality innovation and education to make Indiana one of the nation’s healthiest states. IU Health is among the top ten largest single-state nonprofit health systems in the United States operating 16 hospitals statewide (a mix of urban, suburban and rural facilities). This partnership enables the seamless integration of research findings into patient care. Basic Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in clinical, counseling, or school psychology; social work; public health; neuroscience, or a closely related field. Doctorate or terminal degree preferred, ABD (pending dissertation defense) will be considered for strong candidates. Successful completion of APA -accredited internship, if applicable Prior experience conducting patient-oriented research or clinical trials, alongside a strong background in academic writing and scientific presentations Experience with clinical assessment and therapy, with a strong preference for candidates who have worked with youth and families. Exceptional clinical, analytical, interpersonal, and communication skills Department Contact for Questions Interested candidates are requested to submit the following materials by email ( jalydeck@iu.edu ) to Dr. Janet Lydecker, Associate Professor of Psychiatry and Director of Teen POWER : · CV · A statement of interests · Names of three potential references (reference letters will be requested after initial review) Additional Qualifications Special Instructions The expected start date is summer 2027 (preference for August). Applications will be reviewed beginning December 1, 2026, but will be reviewed until the position is filled. Priority Application Review Deadline 02/28/2027 Expected Start Date 06/01/2027 Posting Number IUSM-02538-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae List Of References Optional Documents Letter of Application Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34644": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Research Scientist Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Research Scientist Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For additional information, please contact Wendy Trueblood Miller at wrtruebl@iu.edu. Posting Details Position Details Title Research Scientist Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Indianapolis School of Nursing Location Indianapolis Position Summary The Indiana University School of Nursing seeks an open rank Research Scientist to support a growing portfolio of funded research focused on our areas of research excellence: Serious Illness Care, Prevention and Health Promotion, Quality of Life and Chronic Condition Management, and Community and Health Systems. This position will play a key role in supporting the School’s research mission and will work collaboratively with IUSON faculty to lead and collaborate on externally-funded research projects. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications: -PhD (Nursing or closely related/complementary field) -Prior post-doctoral training preferred -Demonstrated experience in designing, conducting, implementing, and/or supporting large, externally-funded research projects -Evidence of sustained research dissemination (presentations, publications, etc.) -Demonstrated ability to lead and collaborate on externally funded grants, contracts, and other research initiatives. -Demonstrated success in obtaining external grant funding. Department Contact for Questions Tammy Leone tkleone@iu.edu or 317-274-4157 Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For additional information, please contact Wendy Trueblood Miller at wrtruebl@iu.edu. For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101734-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
