    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/30379": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor  of Clinical Radiology &amp; Imaging Sciences,  Emergency, REMOTE",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant/Associate Professor  of Clinical Radiology &amp; Imaging Sciences,  Emergency, REMOTE Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant/Associate Professor  of Clinical Radiology & Imaging Sciences,  Emergency, REMOTE Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant/Associate Professor  of Clinical Radiology & Imaging Sciences,  Emergency, REMOTE Specific Title Appointment Type Clinical Track Faculty Department IUSM - Radiology & Imaging Sciences Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary Third Shift FULLY REMOTE Emergency Radiologist The Department of Radiology and Imaging Sciences at Indiana University School of Medicine in partnership with Indiana University Health Medical Group is seeking an Emergency Radiologist to join our team. Our Indianapolis-based practice of 35+ Emergency Radiologists is expanding teleradiology services throughout the state and we are looking for candidates interested in a hybrid academic/community practice work environment. The job entails working third shift, a one week on/two weeks off (122 shifts/year) model and offers a wide range of cases from both academic medical centers and community hospitals. Work with a collegial team of ER radiologists and excellent clinical administrative assistants who allow you to focus on patient care rather than answering and making phone calls. Shifts are 9 hours, fully remote and performed from home on a workstation provided by the department.  You will always be working alongside multiple other ER radiologists, including a dedicated ER neuroradiologist and pediatric radiologists, with whom you can share challenging cases. Our workflow is enhanced by custom worklists, availability of ER-centric dictation templates and AI programs such as RadAI which autogenerates impressions. Having the ability to read advanced neuro imaging is a plus but not required. Both clinical and academic track positions are available. Salary and benefits are very competitive. In addition to clinical work, this position involves teaching trainees. The Department hosts robust residency and fellowship training programs. IUSM is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. Indianapolis is the capital and most populous city in the State of Indiana. It is growing economically thanks to a strong corporate base anchored by the life sciences. Indiana is home to one of the largest concentrations of health sciences companies in the nation. Indianapolis has a sophisticated blend of charm and culture with a wonderful balance of business and leisure. The growing residential base is supported by rich amenities and quality of life – the city possesses a variety of professional sports, arts venues and outdoor recreation areas. Residents of this dynamic city, and surrounding suburbs, enjoy leading educational systems and top-ranked universities, paired with a diverse population. Indianapolis International Airport is a top-ranked international airport, being named “Best Airport in North America” by Airports Council International for many years. For additional information on life in Indy: https://faculty.medicine.iu.edu/relocation Basic Qualifications Minimum requirements include DO or MD, eligibility for licensure in Indiana, and Radiology board eligibility. Experience working in a Level 1 trauma center is preferred, but not required. Department Contact for Questions Carla Ewing, Associate Director, HR, IUSM Radiology & Imaging Sciences carewing@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline Expected Start Date Posting Number IUSM-02256-2025 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/30086": {
      "title": "Mid-Career or Senior Tenure Track Faculty Professor, Indianapolis Campus",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Mid-Career or Senior Tenure Track Faculty Professor, Indianapolis Campus Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Mid-Career or Senior Tenure Track Faculty Professor, Indianapolis Campus Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Open positions are available for January 1 start dates. Leadership opportunities aligned with faculty expertise may be available. Applications received by November 1, 2024, will be given priority. The following documents must be submitted on-line to: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/25602 . Letter of application/Cover Letter (2-page limit) Curriculum vitae Statement of Research and Teaching/Personal Statement (5-page limit) outlining achievements and goals in teaching, research, and service e.g. https://academicaffairs.indianapolis.iu.edu/Faculty-Affairs/PromotionTenure/guidelines-and-standards Contact list with six references For additional information, please contact Dr. Janet S. Carpenter (email carpentj@iu.edu or phone 317-278-6065), or Richard Griffin, HR Business Partner (email rilgriff@iu.edu). Additional information may also be found on the web site at: nursing.iu.edu Posting Details Position Details Title Mid-Career or Senior Tenure Track Faculty Professor, Indianapolis Campus Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Indianapolis School of Nursing Location Indianapolis Position Summary Indiana University School of Nursing ( IUSON ) seeks qualified applicants for tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of associate or full professor. We invite applicants who have a record of nationally and/or internationally disseminated and peer reviewed scholarship and emerging or sustained national reputation. IUSON offers a full range of academic programs from BSN to DNP and PhD. IUSON is looking for applicants who will contribute to our commitment to engage the city, state, nation, and beyond through research, teaching, and service, in consideration of the rich diversity of our campus and community. Overall, the candidate’s responsibilities include contributing to IUSON’s research, teaching, and service missions. 1. The candidate is expected to have a record of nationally and/or internationally disseminated and peer reviewed scholarship. For appointment to Associate Professor, applicants must show evidence of an emerging national reputation. For appointment to Full Professor, applicants must show evidence of a sustained national reputation as demonstrated by a well-established and cumulative body of work in rank. The candidate must demonstrate an outstanding scholarly record of research, exhibited by high-impact peer-reviewed publications and a forward-looking, vigorous research agenda that has been continually securing competitive, external funding. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with interdisciplinary teams of interprofessional researchers across clinical and academic settings. 2. The candidate is expected to engage in high-quality teaching and mentoring. . 3. The candidate is expected to actively participate in service at the school, campus, community, and professional levels. Basic Qualifications PhD is required. While a PhD in Nursing Science is preferred, candidates who have earned a PhD in a related field (e.g. public health, health sciences, psychology, sociology) will be considered. Candidates who hold a PhD in Nursing must hold or be eligible for an Indiana RN license. A successful history of external funding (e.g., NIH , HRSA , NLN , PCORI ) is strongly preferred. Appointment to academic rank and salary are dependent on evidence of scholarly, teaching and service achievements. Department Contact for Questions Richard Griffin 317-274-2124 Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Open positions are available for January 1 start dates. Leadership opportunities aligned with faculty expertise may be available. Applications received by November 1, 2024, will be given priority. The following documents must be submitted on-line to: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/25602 . Letter of application/Cover Letter (2-page limit) Curriculum vitae Statement of Research and Teaching/Personal Statement (5-page limit) outlining achievements and goals in teaching, research, and service e.g. https://academicaffairs.indianapolis.iu.edu/Faculty-Affairs/PromotionTenure/guidelines-and-standards Contact list with six references For additional information, please contact Dr. Janet S. Carpenter (email carpentj@iu.edu or phone 317-278-6065), or Richard Griffin, HR Business Partner (email rilgriff@iu.edu). Additional information may also be found on the web site at: nursing.iu.edu For Best Consideration Date Expected Start Date 01/01/2025 Posting Number IU-100975-2024 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/25188": {
      "title": "Asst/Assoc Professor in Actuarial Science/Statistics, Math Education, Pure or Applied",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Asst/Assoc Professor in Actuarial Science/Statistics, Math Education, Pure or Applied Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Asst/Assoc Professor in Actuarial Science/Statistics, Math Education, Pure or Applied Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Asst/Assoc Professor in Actuarial Science/Statistics, Math Education, Pure or Applied Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Indianapolis Department of Mathematics – School of Science Location Indianapolis Position Summary FACULTY POSITION IN MATHEMATICAL SCIENCES Searching at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in Actuarial Science/Statistics, Math Education, Pure or Applied The Department of Mathematical Sciences at IUPUI invites applications for a tenure-track position as an Assistant or Associate Professor in actuarial science (statistics or statistics/probability with experience in actuarial science, financial mathematics, or related fields), mathematics education, pure or applied mathematics to begin on or before August 1, 2024. Responsibilities include teaching six courses over the first two years, with at least one course each term, and then four courses a year regularly, maintaining a strong research program, publishing the results of research, and the customary student advising and departmental and university service. The Department has a strong research faculty, many funded research projects and close collaboration with other departments within the School of Science and the IU School of Medicine. As one of the largest academic units on campus serving more than 13,000 students each year, the Department is central to the mission of IUPUI to advance the State of Indiana and the intellectual growth of its citizens to the highest levels. The appointment is intended to strengthen both research and our graduate programs, and enhance our undergraduate programs (actuarial sciences, mathematics education, pure, applied, and statistics). Current areas of research strength in the Department include mathematical physics and integrable systems, dynamical systems, operator algebras and non-commutative geometry, differential equations/geometry, mathematical neuroscience and biomathematics, scientific computing, statistics, and mathematics education. The School of Science at IUPUI is committed to being an institution that not only reflects the diversity of the learners we teach, but also pursues the values of diversity, equity and inclusion that inform academic excellence. We desire candidates who enhance our representational diversity, as well as those whose work contributes to equitable and inclusive learning and working environments for our students, staff, and faculty. Additional information about the department and programs may be found at https://science.iupui.edu/math/index.html Qualifications: Applicants must have an earned doctorate (at the time of appointment) in statistics, biostatistics, mathematics or related areas, a strong research program, and the ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applicants at the Associate Professor rank will be expected to show an excellent track record of publications, evidence of the ability to engage in independent and/or collaborative (inter)disciplinary research, and existing funding or a high potential for receiving funding from the NSF , NIH or other top tier agencies or organizations. The successful candidates will be expected to maintain an active, externally funded research program. A complete application must include: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statements on research plans and teaching philosophy, and three letters of recommendation. Screening of completed applications will begin on September 1, 2023, and will continue until the position is filled. The IUPUI campus is located near downtown Indianapolis, a city that uniquely combines the cultural amenities of urban life with the residential qualities of smaller communities and is highly affordable. As the major center for industry and government within the state, Indianapolis has a wide variety of research and training sites. Indiana University is an equal employment and affirmative action employer and a provider of ADA services. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, color, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or identity, marital status, national origin, disability status or protected veteran status. Indiana University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment and admission, as required by Title IX. Questions or complaints regarding Title IX may be referred to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights or the university Title IX Coordinator. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here, which includes contact information. The Annual Security Reports, containing policy statements and crime statistics for Indiana University campuses, are available through Public Safety and the IU Police Department web sites at https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html . A paper copy will be provided upon request from Public Safety at iups@iu.edu . As the state’s premier urban research institution, IUPUI is committed to being a welcoming campus community that reflects and enacts the values of diversity, equity and inclusion that inform academic excellence. We seek candidates who will not only enhance our representational diversity but whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to diverse, equitable, and inclusive learning and working environments for our students, staff, and faculty. IUPUI condemns racism in all its forms and has taken an anti-racist stance that moves beyond mere statements to interrogating its policies, procedures, and practices. We hope to identify individuals who will assist in our mission to dismantle racism so that everyone has the opportunity to succeed at IUPUI . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2023, and continue until the position is filled. Basic Qualifications Applicants must have an earned doctorate (at the time of appointment) in statistics, biostatistics, mathematics or related areas, a strong research program, and the ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applicants at the Associate Professor rank will be expected to show an excellent track record of publications, evidence of the ability to engage in independent and/or collaborative (inter)disciplinary research, and existing funding or a high potential for receiving funding from the NSF , NIH or other top tier agencies or organizations. The successful candidates will be expected to maintain an active, externally funded research program. Department Contact for Questions Fang Li email: fali@iupui.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Will be commensurate with experience and qualifications Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 10/01/2023 Expected Start Date 08/01/2024 Posting Number IU-100477-2023 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Statement of Research and Teaching Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34788": {
      "title": "University Archivist",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | University Archivist Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> University Archivist Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title University Archivist Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Indianapolis University Library Location Indianapolis Position Summary IU Indianapolis University Library seeks a University Archivist to join the Ruth Lilly Special Collections and Archives, part of Distinctive Collections. The University Archivist reports to the Director of Distinctive Collections and works collaboratively with library colleagues, faculty, and Indiana University partners to collect and provide access to university records. The position advances institutional priorities related to student and faculty research as well as community engagement and collaboration. This position will work with records of all types, including born-digital records such as websites, emails, and digital files, as well as audio-visual material. The University Archivist will support the full lifecycle of university records, which includes liaising with staff and faculty units about records management policies and the value of institutional records before transfer to the archives, as well as providing education and reference to researchers using these records of permanent value. Responsibilities Actively collect university records deemed of permanent value, including born digital materials and university websites Supervise and perform University Archives collection management activities: accessioning, processing, preservation, and creation of finding aids, including training and supervising student workers to assist in this work Provide reference services for University Archives, assisting virtual and in-person researchers (faculty, students, staff, and other researchers) in using university records Liaise with campus offices on the interpretation and implementation of records retention schedules Manage web archiving of university websites, including appraising URLs and setting appropriate capture schedules Promote interest in the history of IUI / IUPUI and the historic neighborhoods predating the campus, through reference, instruction, and outreach efforts Collaborate with Ruth Lilly Special Collections & Archives department members to improve service, provide access to collections, develop policies and procedures, and move department initiatives forward Secondary responsibilities Participate in development of records management policies in partnership with other campus archivists and the University Records Manager Serve as a member of the Digital Collections Advisory Group, which is charged with setting priorities, establishing best practices for digital collections creation, and evaluating potential digital collections projects Participate in University Library planning and decision-making activities Participate in University Library and campus faculty organizations Represent the library in local, state, and national library venues as appropriate. Participate in library and university initiatives that advance campus and community engagement with distinctive collections Support the mission, vision, values, and strategic priorities of University Library. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree from an ALA -accredited Library/Information Science program or an equivalent degree Minimum 2 years of professional experience in archives, including internships and part-time employment Proven success in archives, including knowledge and experience in archival best practices, principles, and current trends, including born digital records Experience processing large or complex archival collections and creating access tools (finding aids) for these collections Excellent communication, collaboration, and project management skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with a team environment Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of records management Knowledge of web archiving Experience with digital collections, including digital formats and digitization procedures Knowledge of EAD (Encoded Archival Description) Department Contact for Questions Shauna Winter, HR Business Partner, shwint@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101641-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34782": {
      "title": "Research Data Librarian",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Research Data Librarian Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Research Data Librarian Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Research Data Librarian Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Indianapolis University Library Location Indianapolis Position Summary IU Indianapolis University Library seeks a Research Data Librarian to join the Center for Digital Scholarship. Reporting to the Director of the Center for Digital Scholarship, this position collaborates with library colleagues, faculty, and Indiana University partners to support research data management, sharing, discovery, and responsible use across the research lifecycle. The librarian advances institutional research priorities related to open scholarship, compliance, and research impact services. The position contributes to the research information management work of the Center and the strategic priorities of the University Library. Responsibilities Provide consultations on research data management, including data management plans, metadata, storage, sharing, preservation, and repository selection. Support researchers in meeting funder, publisher, and institutional requirements for data sharing and public access. Assist researchers with qualitative and quantitative data discovery and use. Contribute to the development and promotion of research data services, repositories, and data discovery systems. Assist with the ingestion, curation, and management of datasets within an institutional repository. Design and deliver workshops on research data management, data sharing, discovery, and research metrics. Develop and implement outreach strategies for data and research information services. Promote the responsible use of research data, including AI-related considerations. Support faculty and administrators in interpreting research impact data for reporting and planning. Collaborate with liaison librarians and campus partners to integrate research impact and data services into faculty support programs. Advance open scholarship and responsible research practices through participation in library and university initiatives. About Indiana University Indianapolis and University Library IU Indianapolis is an urban-serving institution with a mission and a vision focused on both diversity and community engagement. University Library is a Power of Libraries award winner and home to numerous award-winning professionals. University Library is looking for librarians who will support our commitment to engage with the wider educational community and whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts are inclusive of the rich diversity of our campus and our city. Compensation and Application Minimum salary is $58,000, with additional funding for professional development and travel. Benefits include 22 vacation days, 10 paid holidays, health/dental insurance options, and retirement contributions of 10% to a Fidelity Investments retirement plan. A start-up package includes $10,000 for moving and ongoing professional development expenses. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree from an ALA -accredited Library and Information Science program or equivalent graduate degree. Interest in research data management, sharing, and reuse. Experience or interest in supporting faculty and student researchers. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to adapt to evolving research practices and technologies. Strong library reference interview and database search skills. Knowledge of the higher education research environment, preferably in the social sciences, sciences, or biomedical fields. Preferred Qualifications Project management and cross-functional collaboration experience. Experience supporting a research team or lab with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods. Experience with FAIR , CARE , and best practices in data curation. Experience with research data repositories, metadata, or data discovery systems. Familiarity with reproducible research workflows and scholarly communication issues. Department Contact for Questions Shauna Winter, HR Business Partner shwint@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 08/10/2026 Expected Start Date Posting Number IU-101609-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34776": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Physical Medicine &amp; Rehabilitation",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Physical Medicine &amp; Rehabilitation Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Specific Title Appointment Type Clinical Track Faculty Department IUSM - Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary The Department of Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation at the Indiana University School of Medicine and Indiana University Health Physicians has several openings for Physiatrists in Indianapolis, IN. These positions provide a mixture of inpatient and outpatient clinical rehabilitation care with in-clinic procedures as well as procedures in ambulatory or OR settings. Types of procedures performed include standard PM&R muscular skeletal procedures (e.g., injections, etc.). The faculty member has the opportunity to teach, advise, and mentor the medical students and residents at Indiana University School of Medicine, and publish clinically relevant academic work in peer-reviewed journals. Position includes a joint appointment with IU School of Medicine and IU Health Physicians. IU School of Medicine is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. Indianapolis is the capital and most populous city in the State of Indiana. It is growing economically thanks to a strong corporate base anchored by the life sciences. Indiana is home to one of the nation’s largest concentrations of health sciences companies. Indianapolis has a sophisticated blend of charm and culture with a wonderful balance of business and leisure. The growing residential base is supported by rich amenities and quality of life – the city possesses a variety of professional sports, arts venues, and outdoor recreation areas. Residents of this dynamic city and surrounding suburbs enjoy leading educational systems and top-ranked universities paired with a diverse population. Indianapolis International Airport is a top-ranked international airport that has been named “Best Airport in North America” by Airports Council International for many years. For additional information on life in Indy: https://faculty.medicine.iu.edu/relocation Basic Qualifications Terminal degree or doctorate degree required ; Board certified or Board eligible in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation required; must be eligible for unrestricted Indiana medical license Department Contact for Questions Rebecca Veselka rveselka@iuhealth.org Additional Qualifications To gain final administrative approval, the successful candidate is required to provide verification of credentials and other information required by law, including federally required documentation confirming citizenship or permanent residency of the United States or an authorized alien entitled to be employed in the U.S. for the period of appointment. Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline Expected Start Date Posting Number IUSM-02547-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No Will you now or in the future require employer sponsorship for employment (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Application List Of References Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34775": {
      "title": "Tenured/Tenure-Track Open Rank Faculty Position in Medical Oncology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured/Tenure-Track Open Rank Faculty Position in Medical Oncology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured/Tenure-Track Open Rank Faculty Position in Medical Oncology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured/Tenure-Track Open Rank Faculty Position in Medical Oncology Specific Title Appointment Type Tenure Track Faculty Department IUSM - Bloomington (MSCI) Campus IU School of Medicine Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University School of Medicine, Bloomington ( IUSM -B) invites applications for two, dually employed tenured/tenure-track assistant, associate or full professor positions in the School of Medicine, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Hematology/Oncology, and IU Health Medical Group – in the South Region. We seek candidates to join the Indiana University Simon Comprehensive Cancer Center Clinical Trials Program ( IUSCCC CT) to lead clinical trials research in Bloomington, IN and to provide clinical care to patients in the South Region of IU Health. Candidates with research and clinical expertise in clinical trials with an emphasis on breast, lung, gastrointestinal and benign hematology preferred, however, other areas of medical oncology expertise will be considered. We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives and share important research overlap with IU-Bloomington scholars in other health sciences, while also offering new dimensions that will expand and strengthen the statewide IUSM , IU Health, and IU Simon Comprehensive Cancer Center missions. These 12‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 16th, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at the Indiana University School of Medicine Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the regional campus and academic department and division by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge investigator-initiated clinical and translational research both as a principal investigator and co-investigator, teaching and mentoring medical students and residents; and actively providing service within the academic department/division, regional campus of the IUSM , Indiana University Simon Comprehensive Cancer Center, and university alongside clinical service in the IU Health Medical Group. The senior faculty candidate will be responsible for building the clinical trials program as an extension of the IUSCCC CTO . These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, at the Regional Academic Health Center, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the campus, and the IU Health Medical Group in the South Region of Indiana. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and administrative/professional service. Additionally, individuals hired will have a clinical service expectation to provide patient care in the IU Health Medical Group South, at the IU Health Bloomington Hospital. IU School of Medicine is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), with PhD (or equivalent degree) preferred in addition. They must be able to obtain and maintain a license to practice clinical medicine in the State of Indiana and be American Board Eligible or Board Certified in Oncology and Hematology. Candidates must be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the medical student and medical resident level. Candidates for appointment with tenure must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment with tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 16th and continue until both positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length, identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate/full professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) describing experience and approach to investigator initiated trials and/or translational and preclinical work Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) OPTIONAL Up to three representative scholarly publications Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track pre-tenure positions will only be solicited for those selected for screening interviews. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Applicants should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34713 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Allistair Thompson, thompala@iu.edu , or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN, IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities while fostering a culturally diverse campus environment; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. Indiana University School of Medicine is the largest medical school in the United States, with nine campuses statewide and a nationally recognized commitment to excellence in medical education, research, and patient care. IUSM is a leader in biomedical discovery, clinical and translational research, and innovative approaches to improving human health. The Bloomington campus, the school’s largest regional campus, offers a collaborative academic environment with strong connections to Indiana University’s research enterprise and IU Health. Its location within the Regional Academic Health Center provides unique opportunities to integrate medical education, interdisciplinary research, and clinical practice. The Indiana University Melvin and Bren Simon Comprehensive Cancer Center is Indiana’s only National Cancer Institute ( NCI )-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, a distinction recognizing excellence in basic, clinical, and population-based cancer research, education, and community outreach. The Cancer Center serves as the hub for cancer research across Indiana University, bringing together multidisciplinary investigators dedicated to advancing cancer prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and survivorship. With a robust portfolio of clinical trials, nationally recognized research programs, and strong partnerships with IU School of Medicine and IU Health, the Cancer Center provides exceptional opportunities for collaborative investigation and the translation of scientific discoveries into improved patient outcomes. Indiana University Health South Region is a comprehensive regional healthcare network serving communities throughout south-central Indiana. Anchored by IU Health Bloomington Hospital, the region includes hospitals in Bedford and Paoli, IU Health Morgan, and an extensive network of outpatient and specialty care facilities. Located adjacent to the IU Bloomington campus within the Regional Academic Health Center, IU Health Bloomington Hospital provides advanced clinical services, including comprehensive cancer care, in a collaborative academic healthcare environment. The region’s partnership with IU School of Medicine and the IU Simon Comprehensive Cancer Center offers significant opportunities to expand oncology clinical trials, advance translational research, and increase access to innovative cancer treatments for patients throughout southern Indiana. About the city : Bloomington is a vibrant university town that blends small town charm with big city cultural and athletic events. The surrounding region, featuring nature preserves, National forests, and Indiana’s largest reservoir, offers exceptional outdoor recreation opportunities. Friendly, safe, affordable and welcoming, Bloomington is a gem set in the beautiful rolling hills of southern Indiana. Bloomington’s geographic position illustrates our state’s nickname “Crossroad of America.” It is within a 1 hour drive of Indianapolis, 2 hour drive of Louisville, KY, 3.5 hour of Columbus, OH, and ~4 hour drive to Chicago, IL, St. Louis, MO, and Nashville, TN. Bloomington has a low cost of living relative to entry-level faculty salaries. The community is home to many thriving affinity groups and offers an exceptional selection of cultural, educational, and recreational opportunities. Learn more here: https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/bloomington.html . Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), with PhD (or equivalent degree) preferred in addition. They must be able to obtain and maintain a license to practice clinical medicine in the State of Indiana and be American Board Eligible or Board Certified in Oncology and Hematology. Candidates must be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the medical student and medical resident level. Candidates for appointment with tenure must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment with tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Allistair Thompson, thompala@iu.edu , or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline 11/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IUSM-02541-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Agenda Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Publication 1 Publication 2 Publication 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34770": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Specific Title Appointment Type Scientist Track Faculty Department IUSM - Pediatrics Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary The Herman B Wells Center for Pediatric Research conducts basic science and translational research within the Department of Pediatrics at Indiana University School of Medicine. The Wells Center houses more than 300 faculty investigators, staff, and trainees seeking answers to the most pressing questions related to childhood illness. With the collaboration between scientists and physicians, the center aims to increase knowledge of causes and mechanisms of serious pediatric diseases. Our goal is to develop innovative approaches to the diagnosis and treatment of sick children in Indiana and beyond. The Felton Lab’s current work builds on evidence that autoreactive B cell development and function are altered during T1D progression and that B cells exhibit distinct metabolic phenotypes in autoimmune disease. The lab also investigates immunomodulatory approaches and mechanisms, including type I interferon signaling, and integrates mechanistic research with efforts to understand T1D progression and risk. The Assistant Research Professor will serve as a senior scientific member of the Felton lab, supporting and advancing a translational research program focused on the immunologic and metabolic mechanisms underlying type 1 diabetes. The position will have particular responsibility for developing and executing studies examining B cell tolerance, immune cell metabolism, type I interferon signaling, and interactions between immune cells and the pancreatic islet microenvironment. Working closely with the PI, the Assistant Research Professor will provide intellectual and technical leadership for ongoing and emerging projects, including the design and execution of experiments, interpretation and integration of complex datasets, development of new experimental approaches, and preparation of manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, and grant applications. The individual will be expected to exercise substantial scientific independence while contributing to the laboratory’s broader research strategy. The position will also provide day-to-day scientific leadership within the laboratory, including mentoring trainees and research staff, troubleshooting experimental approaches, establishing rigorous and reproducible laboratory practices, and coordinating projects and collaborations. The Assistant Research Professor may lead defined research projects and develop complementary areas of investigation that strengthen the laboratory’s overall research portfolio. This position and scientific environment is particularly suited for an applicant with expertise in immunology, B cell biology, or autoimmunity. IUSM is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. Basic Qualifications Ph.D. in Medical Science, Molecular Biology, immunology, or a related science field. Strong work ethic, high level of motivation, and commitment to scientific excellence. Excellent organizational, communication, and teamwork skills. Department Contact for Questions Dr. Jamie Felton jamifelt@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline Expected Start Date Posting Number IUSM-02545-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34769": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Specific Title Appointment Type Scientist Track Faculty Department IUSM - Pediatrics Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary The Herman B Wells Center for Pediatric Research conducts basic science and translational research within the Department of Pediatrics at Indiana University School of Medicine. The Wells Center houses more than 300 faculty investigators, staff, and trainees seeking answers to the most pressing questions related to childhood illness. With the collaboration between scientists and physicians, the center aims to increase knowledge of causes and mechanisms of serious pediatric diseases. Our goal is to develop innovative approaches to the diagnosis and treatment of sick children in Indiana and beyond. Research in the DeRyckere and Graham labs focuses on the TAM -family tyrosine kinase receptors and their roles as potential therapeutic targets in the immune system and in cancer cells. Our goal is to develop new therapies for treatment of cancer in children and adults and we are actively engaged in development of novel drugs. In conjunction with this work, we also develop and apply next-generation model systems to advance our research and for precision medicine applications. Our lab is a fast-paced, collegial and supportive research environment. The DeRyckere and Graham labs are seeking a full-time Assistant Research Professor to lead a project focused on the TAM family kinases as therapeutic targets for treatment of breast cancer. Responsibilities will include experimental design and execution, data analysis and presentation, preparation of federal grant applications and reports, teaching and supervising students and trainees. This position is expected to comprise 65% lab research and data analysis, 25% reading and writing grants/manuscripts/presentations and 10% teaching/mentoring junior scientists. The ideal candidate will be a dynamic individual who is able to work independently to manage and complete multiple projects/tasks simultaneously. IUSM is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. Basic Qualifications Doctorate or Terminal degree required Department Contact for Questions Deb DeRyckere debderyc@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline Expected Start Date Posting Number IUSM-02546-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34752": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor of Anatomy, Cell Biology &amp; Physiology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Research Professor of Anatomy, Cell Biology &amp; Physiology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Research Professor of Anatomy, Cell Biology & Physiology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Research Professor of Anatomy, Cell Biology & Physiology Specific Title Appointment Type Scientist Track Faculty Department IUSM - Anatomy, Cell Biology & Physiology Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary The Sankar Laboratory and the Department of Anatomy, Cell Biology & Physiology at Indiana University School of Medicine are seeking a highly motivated Research Scientist to lead studies within a newly funded NIH project investigating cell-intrinsic pain mechanisms in osteoarthritis (OA). This interdisciplinary project will use global and conditional knockout mouse models to investigate sensory neuron and joint cell-intrinsic roles of Ca2+/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase kinase 2 (CAMKK2) in OA pain using single-cell RNA sequencing and spatial transcriptomics of the joint. The project will also employ cutting-edge 3D light-sheet microscopy to map sensory neuron dynamics and inflammation during OA progression and mechanistic signaling studies in the dorsal root ganglion. Applicants should hold a PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent degree in musculoskeletal biology, neuroscience, immunology, molecular biology, or a related field. We seek a passionate, self-driven, and collaborative scientist with relevant postdoctoral or equivalent research experience and demonstrated expertise in OA, musculoskeletal and single cell transcriptomics, transgenic mouse models and colony management, animal surgery or behavioral phenotyping, molecular signaling, advanced microscopy, and bioinformatics. Experience in pain research is desirable but not required. Fluency in spoken and written English is required. The successful candidate is expected to drive research projects with a high degree of independence, analyze and integrate complex datasets, contribute to manuscripts and grant applications, and mentor junior laboratory members. Candidates will be considered based on their overall experience, scientific productivity, technical expertise, and potential to advance this interdisciplinary program. The Scientist will join the Indiana Center for Musculoskeletal Health, a vibrant and supportive multidisciplinary community offering outstanding collaborative opportunities and access to advanced genomics, imaging, computational, and animal research resources. Located in Indianapolis, Indiana University School of Medicine provides a highly collaborative biomedical research environment in an affordable and dynamic city with a growing life sciences sector and excellent quality of life. Please apply with a cover letter of interest, along with a detailed CV, copies of any relevant publications, and names/addresses of three references. IU School of Medicine is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana.\" Indianapolis is the capital and most populous city in the State of Indiana. It is growing economically thanks to a strong corporate base anchored by the life sciences. Indiana is home to one of the largest concentrations of health sciences companies in the nation. Indianapolis has a sophisticated blend of charm and culture with a wonderful balance of business and leisure. The growing residential base is supported by rich amenities and quality of life – the city possesses a variety of professional sports, arts venues and outdoor recreation areas. Residents of this dynamic city, and surrounding suburbs, enjoy leading educational systems and top-ranked universities, paired with a diverse population. Indianapolis International Airport is a top-ranked international airport, being named “Best Airport in North America” by Airports Council International for many years. Information about the Department of Anatomy, Cell Biology & Physiology is available at: https://medicine.iu.edu/anatomy-cell-biology-physiology Information about the Indiana University School of Medicine is available at: https://medicine.iu.edu Basic Qualifications PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent degree in musculoskeletal biology, neuroscience, immunology, molecular biology, or a related field Department Contact for Questions Dr. Uma Sankar ( usankar@iu.edu ) Additional Qualifications Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline Expected Start Date Posting Number IUSM-02543-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Publication 1 Publication 2 Optional Documents Publication 3 Publication 4 Publication 5 Publication 6 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34751": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Research Professor of Pediatrics Specific Title Appointment Type Scientist Track Faculty Department IUSM - Pediatrics Campus IU School of Medicine Indianapolis Position Summary The Herman B Wells Center for Pediatric Research conducts basic science and translational research within the Department of Pediatrics at Indiana University School of Medicine. The Wells Center houses more than 200 faculty investigators, staff, and trainees seeking answers to the most pressing questions related to childhood illness. With the collaboration between scientists and physicians, the center aims to increase knowledge of causes and mechanisms of serious pediatric diseases. Our goal is to develop innovative approaches to the diagnosis and treatment of sick children in Indiana and beyond. An Assistant Research Professor in this position is expected to provide leadership within the laboratory on scientific methods and practices for immunology and genetic measurements to determine risk or presence of Type 1 diabetes in human clinical research. This includes developing new techniques to measure relevant biomarkers, including methods using radioisotopes and quality control programs. This role will also provide leadership in obtaining and maintaining regulatory approval for performance, reporting and use of disease-related biomarkers. This role will provide support for writing reports, grants and academic manuscripts related to the work of the laboratory. We seek to study Type 1 diabetes and related autoimmune diseases, using measurements of antibodies, genes, metabolic signals, and related biomarkers. These are typically used in large clinical research studies to demonstrate efficient methods for identifying subjects at risk and/or for identifying triggering environmental exposures. The lab works on studies led by Dr. Hagopian, led by other IU investigators, or led by collaborating academic investigators at other institutions. The lab also maintains a biosample bank from Dr. Hagopian’s historical studies which can be used to investigate biomarkers of disease. IUSM is committed to being a welcoming campus community and we seek candidates whose research, teaching, and community engagement efforts contribute to robust learning and working environments for all students, staff, and faculty. We invite individuals who will join us in our mission to improve health equity and well-being for all throughout the state of Indiana. Basic Qualifications Ph.D. in Biochemistry or a related biomedical/science field. Department Contact for Questions Dr. William Hagopian bhagopia@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Special Instructions Priority Application Review Deadline Expected Start Date Posting Number IUSM-02528-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Personal Contact: School of Medicine recruiter Personal Contact: IUHP Physician Recruiter Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Are you a dual career partner (your partner or spouse is already being recruited)? Yes No Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
